# Raw training curves: 245 MB across 562 files, and they are DERIVED data —
# every figure and every scored statistic is reproducible from the results
# JSONL plus the harness. Committing them would make the repo unclonable for
# the reviewers who most want to check it.
#
# NOT ignored, deliberately: results/results/*.jsonl (300 KB, the scored data)
# and results/logs/ (2.4 MB, carries the per-job node provenance the paper
# reports). Those two are the audit trail and must be in history.
#
# If curves are needed for release, publish them as a versioned archive
# (Zenodo / GitHub Release asset) and cite the DOI in the paper.
results/results/curves_*.csv

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
*.bak-*
.expected_md5
.venv

# Same policy for pilot curves and the archived, unscored E19 run-1 curves:
# derived data, reproducible from the JSONL rows + harness; too large to commit.
results/pilots_e17/curves_*.csv
results/pilots_e17/**/curves_*.csv
results/results/e19_run1_unscorable/curves/
